! sw1 — EtherChannel practice switch  (Arista EOS)
!
! LACP Port-Channel configuration practice.
! Ethernet1 and Ethernet2 are the two links to sw2 that will form the bundle.
! Ethernet3 connects to host1 (pre-configured).
!
! YOUR TASK: Configure LACP EtherChannel between sw1 and sw2
!
! Step 1 — Create the Port-Channel interface:
!   configure
!   interface Port-Channel1
!      description to sw2 (LACP bundle)
!      no switchport
!      ip address 10.12.0.1/30
!
! Step 2 — Add physical members (LACP active mode):
!   interface Ethernet1
!      channel-group 1 mode active
!   interface Ethernet2
!      channel-group 1 mode active
!
! Step 3 — Verify:
!   show etherchannel summary
!   show etherchannel detail
!   show interfaces Port-Channel1
!   ping 10.12.0.2                   <- sw2 Port-Channel IP
!   ping 10.0.1.2                    <- host2 (after OSPF or static route)
!
! LACP modes:
!   active  — initiates LACP negotiation (prefer this on both sides)
!   passive — responds to LACP negotiation (will not initiate)
!   on      — static bundle, no LACP negotiation (must be "on" on both sides)
!
! Load-balancing (global setting):
!   port-channel load-balance src-dst-mac    <- default for L2
!   port-channel load-balance src-dst-ip     <- use for routed traffic
!
hostname sw1
!
interface Loopback0
   ip address 10.0.0.1/32
!
interface Ethernet1
   description to sw2 link-1 (future Port-Channel1 member)
   no switchport
   ! YOUR TASK: Add channel-group 1 mode active
!
interface Ethernet2
   description to sw2 link-2 (future Port-Channel1 member)
   no switchport
   ! YOUR TASK: Add channel-group 1 mode active
!
interface Ethernet3
   description to host1
   no switchport
   ip address 10.0.1.253/24
!
ip routing
!
! YOUR TASK: Create Port-Channel1 with ip address 10.12.0.1/30
!
end
